{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Explain what happens in a commutation failure.",say:'Question one. Explain what happens in a commutation failure.',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'Explain what happens'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Explain what happens in a commutation failure.",say:'The outgoing thyristor has not recovered when its voltage turns positive, so it conducts again. The incoming one turns off, and two thyristors of one leg conduct. The DC source is shorted through the bridge, and the current rises sharply.',cues:{a1:'The outgoing thyristor',a2:'The incoming one',a3:'The DC source is'},al:[["The outgoing thyristor has not recovered when its voltage turns positive, so it conducts again.",'a1'],["The incoming one turns off; two thyristors of one leg conduct.",'a2'],["The DC source is shorted through the bridge, so the current rises sharply.",'a3']],vis:(c,u,b)=>
 g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),PE_T(30,40,'γ shorter than ωtq',{fs:24,fw:800,fill:TRED})+PE_bar(30,590,62,46,[[158,BLU,'α'],[17,ORG,'μ'],[5,TRED,'']])+PE_L(Math.round(30+560*170/180),134,589,134,MAG,4)+PE_T(Math.round(30+560*170/180)-8,142,'ωtq',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'end',fill:MAG}))
 +g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),PE_leg(150,270,TRED)+PE_L(150,208,380,208,'#18213A',3)+PE_L(150,332,380,332,'#18213A',3)+PE_L(380,208,380,258,'#18213A',3)+PE_bat(380,270,MAG,1)+PE_L(380,282,380,332,'#18213A',3)+PE_T(408,278,'E',{fs:26,fw:800,fill:MAG})
  +PE_arrow(240,224,300,224,TRED,4)+PE_arrow(300,316,240,316,TRED,4)+PE_T(60,252,'both',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:TRED})+PE_T(60,280,'on',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:TRED}))
 +g('pop',tk(c,'a3'),PE_L(40,470,590,470,PE_GR,2)+PE_L(40,470,40,360,PE_GR,2)+`<polyline points="40,440 300,440 330,430 360,410 390,380 410,358" fill="none" stroke="${TRED}" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>`+PE_T(48,430,'Id',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:PE_MU})+PE_T(430,400,'rises sharply',{fs:24,fw:800,fill:TRED})+PE_T(590,500,'time',{fs:22,a:'end',fill:PE_MU}))},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A single-phase bridge on 230 V, 50 Hz has Ls = 2 mH (total) and Id = 10 A. Find ΔVd and μ at α = 0.",say:'Question two. A single-phase bridge: two hundred thirty volts, fifty hertz, two millihenries in total, ten amps. Find the drop, and mu at zero firing angle.',cues:{k:'Question two',q:'A single-phase bridge'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A single-phase bridge on 230 V, 50 Hz has Ls = 2 mH (total) and Id = 10 A. Find ΔVd and μ at α = 0.",say:'Omega L is zero point six two eight ohms. Two times that, times ten, over pi: a drop of four volts. Then cosine mu is zero point nine six one four, so mu is sixteen degrees.',cues:{fk:'Omega L is',k1:'Omega L is zero',k2:'Two times that',k2b:'a drop of four',k3:'Then cosine mu',k3b:'so mu is sixteen'},calc:{f:['ΔVd = 2ωLs Id / π','cos μ = 1 − 2ωLs Id / Vm'],hint:'Vm = √2 × 230 = 325.27 V; at α = 0, cos α = 1.',fk:'fk',steps:[["ωLs","314.16 × 0.002 = 0.6283 Ω","k1"],["ΔVd",["2 × 0.6283 × 10 / π","ΔVd = 4.0 V"],["k2","k2b"]],["μ",["cos μ = 1 − 12.566 / 325.27 = 0.9614","μ = 16.0°"],["k3","k3b"]]],live:[0,1,2]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Why is the overlap angle smaller at α = 60° than at α = 0 for the same current?",say:'Question three. Why is the overlap angle smaller at sixty degrees than at zero, for the same current?',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'Why is the overlap'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Why is the overlap angle smaller at α = 60° than at α = 0 for the same current?",say:'The transfer needs a fixed volt-second area, two omega L times the current. Near ninety degrees the commutating voltage peaks, so that area fills a smaller angle: twelve point one degrees at zero, one point four six at sixty.',cues:{a1:'The transfer needs',a2:'Near ninety degrees',a3:'twelve point one'},al:[["The transfer needs a fixed volt-second area, 2ωLs Id.",'a1'],["Near α = 90° the commutating voltage peaks, so the area fits a smaller angle.",'a2'],["Worked example: μ = 12.1° at α = 0, only 1.46° at α = 60°.",'a3']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{
 const f=t=>Math.sin(PE_rad(t)),X=d=>40+540*d/180;
 return g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),PE_T(30,40,'commutating voltage, line peak √2 VL',{fs:22,fw:700,fill:PE_MU})+PE_L(40,400,590,400,PE_GR,2)+PE_area(f,0,12.1,0,180,40,580,400,300,BLU,.6)+PE_curve(f,0,180,40,580,400,300,BLU,4)
   +PE_T(X(6),440,'α = 0',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU})+PE_T(86,386,'μ = 12.1°',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:BLU}))
  +g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),PE_L(X(90),100,X(90),400,PE_MU,2,'stroke-dasharray="6 6"')+`<circle cx="${X(90)}" cy="100" r="10" fill="${ORG}"/>`+PE_T(X(90)+18,92,'peak at 90°',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:ORG}))
  +g('pop',tk(c,'a3'),PE_area(f,60,61.46,0,180,40,580,400,300,ORG,.95)+PE_L(X(60.7),400-300*f(60.7),X(60.7),400,ORG,6)+PE_T(X(60),440,'α = 60°',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:ORG})+PE_arrow(330,210,X(61.5)+6,240,ORG,3)+PE_T(336,204,'μ = 1.46°',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:ORG})+PE_T(310,490,'same area 2ωLs Id in both',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:INK}))}},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:'Your free notes are the PDF linked in the description. Redraw the overlap waveforms and the inverter limit curves from memory, then check them.',cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the overlap'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["In this lesson", "Effect of source inductance; inversion mode and the inverter angle limit"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["The overlap waveforms", "230 V bridge, Ls = 5 mH, Id = 20 A, α = 30°: for μ = 17.7° after each firing vo = 0 and is ramps from −20 A to +20 A."], ["The inverter limit curves", "400 V bridge, Ls = 1 mH, γ0 = 15°: overlap lowers Vdc by 6 V at 20 A and 30 V at 100 A; the curves stop at 160.7° and 148.7°."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: Mohan, Undeland and Robbins (Power Electronics: Converters, Applications, and Design); Muhammad H. Rashid (Power Electronics: Circuits, Devices, and Applications); P. S. Bimbhra (Power Electronics)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:'So remember: source inductance makes the current overlap, overlap costs volts, and an inverter must finish its overlap a safe margin before one hundred eighty degrees. Next time, dual converters. See you there!',cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'source inductance makes',w2:'overlap costs volts',w3:'and an inverter must',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['THE CURRENT OVERLAPS','BLU','w1'],['OVERLAP COSTS VOLTS','ORG','w2'],['α + μ ≤ 180° − γ₀','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next lesson", "Dual converters", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
